}>{"not a virtue."}</em></h1><p className={"custom-ph-lead max-w-136 text-[clamp(1.0625rem,1rem_+_0.3vw,1.25rem)] leading-[1.65] text-soft text-pretty"} data-anim={"fade-up"} data-anim-delay={"140"}>{"Six years is not a slow hold. It is the time it takes to hire well, buy well and leave a company stronger than we found it."}</p></div></div><div className={"container"}><figure className={"custom-ph-media aspect-[16/10] mt-[clamp(3rem,2rem_+_3vw,5rem)] overflow-clip rounded-(--custom-radius-panel) bg-soft md:aspect-[21/9]"} data-anim={"fade-up"} data-anim-delay={"220"} data-anim-duration={"1200"}><img className={"size-full object-cover"} src={"https://draftmango.com/framo/assets/media/placeholder/2880x1234.svg"} alt={"Two partners talking by the window of a quiet boardroom above London at dawn"} width={"2880"} height={"1620"} fetchPriority={"high"} decoding={"async"} style={{"objectPosition": "55% 50%"}} /></figure></div></section><section id={"i1-ar-essay"} className={"custom-section"} aria-label={"The essay"}><div className={"container grid grid-cols-1 gap-y-10 gap-x-[clamp(2.5rem,4vw,4rem)] lg:grid-cols-[minmax(14rem,1fr)_minmax(0,42rem)_minmax(0,0.6fr)]"}><aside className={"lg:sticky lg:top-32 lg:[align-self:start]"} aria-label={"About this essay"} data-anim={"fade-up"}><p className={"flex items-center gap-3.5 m-0 leading-[1.4] text-soft"}><img className={"flex-none size-12 rounded-full object-cover object-[50%_15%] bg-(--custom-mark)"} src={"https://draftmango.com/framo/assets/media/placeholder/600x800.svg"} alt={""} width={"96"} height={"96"} loading={"lazy"} decoding={"async"} /><span><strong className={"block font-semibold text-text"}>{"James Whitfield"}</strong>{" Partner, Private Equity"}</span></p><dl className={"custom-ar-facts grid mt-7"}><div><dt className={"text-(--custom-muted)"}>{"Published"}</dt><dd><time datetime={"2026-09-14"}>{"14 September 2026"}</time></dd></div><div><dt className={"text-(--custom-muted)"}>{"Topic"}</dt><dd>{"Outlook"}</dd></div><div><dt className={"text-(--custom-muted)"}>{"Reading Time"}</dt><dd>{"7 min"}</dd></div></dl><div className={"social-share mt-7"}><span className={"social-share-label"}>{"Share"}</span><ul className={"social-list"} role={"list"}><li><button type={"button"} className={"btn btn-circle btn-copy"} data-copy-url={""} data-copy-done={"Link copied"} aria-label={"Copy the link to this essay"}><i className={"ph ph-link"} aria-hidden={"true"}></i><span className={"sr-only"} data-copy-label={""} aria-live={"polite"}></span></button></li><li><a href={"#"} className={"social-link social-link--circle social-link--soft"} aria-label={"Share on LinkedIn"}><i className={"ph ph-linkedin-logo"} aria-hidden={"true"}></i></a></li><li><a href={"mailto:?subject=Why%20patience%20is%20a%20strategy"} className={"social-link social-link--circle social-link--soft"} aria-label={"Share by email"}><i className={"ph ph-envelope-simple"} aria-hidden={"true"}></i></a></li></ul></div></aside><article className={"custom-ar-body min-w-0"}><p className={"custom-ar-first"}>{"Every few years someone asks us why we hold companies for so long. The question usually comes with a spreadsheet attached, showing how much better the returns would look if we sold in year three. The spreadsheet is never wrong. It simply measures the wrong thing."}</p><p>{"A business does not become more valuable because time passes. It becomes more valuable because people inside it make hundreds of good decisions, most of them small, and each one needs a little room to pay off. A new head of sales needs a year to rebuild a team. A second factory needs two. An acquisition needs three before it feels like one company. None of that fits neatly into an investment memo, and all of it shows up in the price a buyer is willing to pay."}</p><h2>{"The arithmetic of time"}</h2><p>{"Since 1995 we have held our companies for a little over six years on average. That is longer than most of our peers, and we have been told more than once that it costs us. We do not think it does. A longer hold lets a management team plan for the business rather than for the sale, and it lets us be choosy about who buys it next."}</p><p>{"It also changes the conversations we have with founders. When a founder knows we will not be looking for an exit in the second year, they tell us what they really want to build. More often than not, it is something bigger than the plan they came in with."}</p><figure className={"custom-ar-figure mt-[clamp(2.5rem,2rem_+_2vw,3.5rem)] mb-[clamp(2.5rem,2rem_+_2vw,3.5rem)] xl:w-[calc(100%_+_10rem)]"}><img className={"w-full rounded-(--custom-radius-card) bg-soft"} src={"https://draftmango.com/framo/assets/media/placeholder/1400x788.svg"} alt={"A management team and a partner mapping a hundred-day plan on a whiteboard"} width={"1400"} height={"788"} loading={"lazy"} decoding={"async"} /><figcaption className={"mt-3.5 text-[0.9375rem] leading-[1.5] text-(--custom-muted)"}>{"The first hundred days: the plan is written with the management team, never handed to it."}</figcaption></figure><h2>{"What six years buys"}</h2><p>{"Patience is not the same as waiting. Every company we own has a plan agreed within its first hundred days, a board that meets monthly and an operating partner who has done the work before. The years are full. They are simply not hurried."}</p><figure className={"custom-ar-ledger mt-[clamp(2.5rem,2rem_+_2vw,3.5rem)] mb-[clamp(2.5rem,2rem_+_2vw,3.5rem)] p-[clamp(1.5rem,1rem_+_2vw,2.5rem)] rounded-(--custom-radius-card) bg-(--custom-card)"}><figcaption className={"mb-3 font-heading text-[1.375rem] italic text-primary-ink"}>{"The portfolio, 1995–2025"}</figcaption><dl className={"custom-ledger"}><div className={"custom-ledger-row"}><dt className={"custom-ledger-label"}>{"Average holding period"}</dt><dd className={"custom-ledger-value"}>{"6.2 years"}</dd></div><div className={"custom-ledger-row"}><dt className={"custom-ledger-label"}>{"Plan agreed"}</dt><dd className={"custom-ledger-value"}>{"Within 100 days"}</dd></div><div className={"custom-ledger-row"}><dt className={"custom-ledger-label"}>{"Add-ons per company"}</dt><dd className={"custom-ledger-value"}>{"2.4 on average"}</dd></div><div className={"custom-ledger-row"}><dt className={"custom-ledger-label"}>{"Gross realised multiple"}</dt><dd className={"custom-ledger-value"}>{"3.1x"}</dd></div></dl></figure><p>{"The numbers matter, but the shape behind them matters more. Most of the value in our realised companies was made in years three to six, after the new people had settled and the add-ons had been joined up. Selling earlier would have meant selling a promise. Selling later lets us sell a result."}</p><blockquote className={"custom-ar-quote mt-[clamp(3rem,2.5rem_+_2vw,4.5rem)] mb-[clamp(3rem,2.5rem_+_2vw,4.5rem)] py-[clamp(2rem,1.5rem_+_1.5vw,3rem)]"}><p className={"font-heading text-[clamp(1.75rem,1.3rem_+_1.6vw,2.625rem)] leading-[1.2] tracking-[-0.015em] text-text text-balance"}>{"Selling earlier would have meant selling a promise. "}<em className={"text-primary-ink"}>{"Selling later lets us sell a result."}</em></p></blockquote><h2>{"When to step aside"}</h2><figure className={"custom-ar-figure custom-ar-figure--aside my-[clamp(2.5rem,2rem_+_2vw,3.5rem)] mx-0 sm:mt-[0.4rem] sm:mb-6 sm:mr-0 sm:ml-8 sm:w-[44%]"}><img className={"w-full rounded-(--custom-radius-card) bg-soft aspect-[4/3] object-cover object-[50%_60%] sm:aspect-[4/5] sm:object-cover"} src={"https://draftmango.com/framo/assets/media/placeholder/900x1200.svg"} alt={"Two investors meeting a company's managers in a workshop office, a wall of notes behind"} width={"900"} height={"1200"} loading={"lazy"} decoding={"async"} /><figcaption className={"mt-3.5 text-[0.9375rem] leading-[1.5] text-(--custom-muted)"}>{"Buyers meet the team long before the sale."}</figcaption></figure><p>{"The hardest part of patience is knowing when it has run its course. We start planning the sale in the first year, not because we are in a hurry, but because the right next owner is worth looking for. When Corvex was sold in 2025, the buyer wanted the team as much as the software. That was the point."}</p><p>{"None of this makes us slow. It makes us deliberate. We would rather do fewer things properly and hand on companies that keep growing after we have gone. That, in the end, is the only measure of ownership we trust."}</p><p className={"custom-ar-sign mt-10 italic text-soft"}>{"— James Whitfield, London"}</p></article></div></section><section id={"i1-ar-author"} className={"custom-section"} aria-labelledby={"i1-ar-author-name"}><div className={"container"}><aside className={"custom-ar-author-card sm:grid-cols-[minmax(0,13rem)_minmax(0,1fr)]"} data-anim={"fade-up"}><svg className={"custom-rings custom-ar-author-rings"} viewBox={"0 0 600 600"} fill={"none"} aria-hidden={"true"} focusable={"false"}><g className={"custom-rings-turn"}><path d={"M309 312C309 314 309 316 309 318C308 320 307 322 305 324C304 326 302 327 300 328C298 330 297 331 295 332C293 333 291 334 289 335C287 335 284 335 282 335C280 335 277 335 275 334C273 334 271 333 269 332C267 331 266 329 264 328C263 327 261 325 260 323C259 322 258 320 257 318C256 316 256 314 256 312C256 310 256 308 257 306C257 304 258 302 259 300C260 298 261 296 262 294C264 293 266 292 268 291C271 290 273 290 275 290C278 289 280 289 282 290C284 290 286 290 288 291C290 291 292 292 294 293C296 294 298 295 300 296C302 297 303 299 304 300C306 302 307 304 307 306C308 308 309 310 309 312Z"}></path><path d={"M334 311C334 315 333 319 332 322C331 326 329 330 326 333C324 336 321 339 317 341C314 344 311 346 308 348C304 350 300 352 296 353C292 354 288 354 284 354C280 354 276 353 272 351C268 350 264 349 260 347C257 346 253 344 250 341C247 338 245 335 243 332C241 329 240 325 239 322C237 318 236 315 236 311C236 307 236 303 237 299C237 296 238 292 240 288C242 285 244 281 248 278C251 275 255 273 259 272C263 270 267 270 272 270C276 269 280 269 284 269C288 269 292 270 296 271C300 272 303 273 307 